"""Curated tables for the Technology, food and energy workstream.

Each invention or crop has an origin and a list of diffusion steps. One step = one place and one year,
read as "this technology was in use (or this crop was grown) here by this year". Steps are claims a
historian can check, so each carries a note, and a step can carry its own source when it differs from
the record's. Years are first-attestation years, not "invented on this day" dates; `a` marks a rough one.

Places: (slug, name, lat, lon). Existing kernel ids (place:mainz, place:venice...) are reused; the build
writes a stub for every place it uses, so the owner's record wins on merge.
"""

W = lambda t: {"cite": f"Wikipedia: {t}", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/" + t.replace(" ", "_")}

